WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
An optician hands you a lens.

2
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:04.670
It is not labelled with its focal length.

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.890
It is labelled plus 4.

4
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.940
That number is the lens's
power, measured in dioptres.

5
00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.930
A shorter focal length
means a bigger number.

6
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.290
A more strongly curved
lens has a larger power.

7
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.170
A diverging lens has a negative power.

8
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.600
But why bother?

9
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.010
Why describe a lens by its power,
and not simply by its focal length?

10
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.080
In this mission, you'll work out a
lens's power from its focal length,

11
00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.610
with the right sign.

12
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.560
Then you'll place two
thin lenses in contact,

13
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.240
and find out what the pair does together.

14
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: explain why opticians
describe a lens by its power.
